xmodel/exact-coframe-background-review-grok-20260824.md:122:checked identically. Thus `U ∈ E_2(C) ⊂ E_2(S)` conjugates `E_2(S)` to itself because `E_2(S)` is a subgroup. Scalar conjugation is trivial. Feasibility’s square-root factorization `C = λ U` is available over `C` and is unnecessary: the diagonal reduction works over any field.
xmodel/exact-coframe-background-review-grok-20260824.md:132:The converse — `J(P,Q) ∈ E_2 ⇒ (P,Q)` is an automorphism — is **not** part of the reviewed statement. The root card, the adversary (§3.1), and the feasibility report all warn that `M ∈ E_2` is not an automorphy certificate. That warning is **in tension with Wright 1978**, cited as standard by Drensky–Yu 2001: if the Jacobian of an endomorphism lies in `GE_2`, then the endomorphism is an automorphism (“weak Jacobian theorem”). The primary Wright PDF was not retrieved in this session (ScienceDirect blocked; DOI `10.1016/0022-4049(78)90003-8` from the 1978 JPAA pagination). Until that paper is read, the converse remains a **GAP**. The reviewed one-way implication does not use it.
xmodel/exact-coframe-background-review-grok-20260824.md:140:`E_2(S)` is a subgroup of `SL_2(S)`. For `n = 2` it is not automatically normal (Costa–Keller, *On the normal subgroups of SL(2,A)*, J. Pure Appl. Algebra 53 (1988) 201–226; announcement Bull. AMS 24 (1991) 131–135). The root card’s language “class in `SL_2/E_2`” and “nontrivial Mennicke class” is therefore unsafe as group-quotient language. The adversary and feasibility corrections are right: the certificate is plain nonmembership `M ∉ E_2(S)`.
xmodel/exact-coframe-background-review-grok-20260824.md:254:plus a 6-dimensional homogeneous space. Along the corresponding one-parameter word, `[ε^0]κ + [ε^1]κ = 0`, while `[ε^2]κ` is nonzero, and no choice of the six free parameters kills `[ε^2]`. So this cheapest linearized-nonempty family does not lift to second order in a formal neighbourhood of `C`.
xmodel/exact-coframe-background-review-grok-20260824.md:281:The synthesis ranking that assigned this root a “direct characteristic-zero counterexample” payoff at a small bounded orbit overstated the positive branch. The coordinator applied the Moh/GGV bound to demote the degree-three local scheme and did not apply it to the exact-coframe family. The bound applies to *any* explicit plane Keller pair.
xmodel/exact-coframe-background-review-grok-20260824.md:330:Stop the exact-coframe root, without support expansion, on any of:
xmodel/exact-coframe-background-review-grok-20260824.md:346:Not reviewed except as named conflicts: the other eleven idea fingerprints of the round; D-series, Witt, books, TRACE, passports, HC4, Dixmier, GGV farm mathematics beyond the degree ceiling; the finite-normalization / class-group root; the weighted `D` quotient; AUDIT claims other than the observation that none of them is an `E_2` theorem; Wright 1978 primary PDF (blocked); the HKU Drensky–Yu PDF (Cloudflare-blocked; page-521 sentence recovered from the public full-text index of that bitstream); a generic sparse Gröbner run of the 24-parameter family (licensed as a later instrument, not executed here); any claim that emptiness of one bounded orbit proves JC2.
